What’s with all the hype about the 2021 era of TDS? I have seen too many people claim that this era of the game was one of the best, completely ignoring the massive issues and only supporting their points with ‘nostalgia and that the game is really just corporate slop right now’. If you were actually around earlier, you would know that back in like 2022-2023, 2021 was seen as the worst year for the game or close it, and once you look more into it, it’s not exactly hard to understand why.&nbsp;

THE ISSUES
The Balancing of the Game’s Towers
If you were around for most of the Overhaul - Solar Eclipse era, you probably remember that the balancing of the game was atrociously bad, this trend started in the Overhaul update. Half of the towers were made useless, with extremely expensive costs just to contribute nothing.&nbsp;

One clear example of this was Mortar and Rocketeer in Pre-Overhaul, two towers you were really required to use to get past the shielded enemies with a damage cap. When the Overhaul update dropped, the shield damage cap mechanic was completely removed, that change itself isn’t necessarily bad, but both tower’s stats were nerfed to barely being usable.&nbsp;

The Overhaul Update did start this, but Frost Invasion did not make it any better. You have the Militant rework which the devs said would make the tower better… by adding a very limiting ammo system. Solar Eclipse brought along the Hunter rework which changed pretty much nothing.&nbsp;

Obviously, every tower defense game is going to have its meta, which is completely normal. My main point here is that 2021 TDS has so many useless shop obtainable towers. Comparing it to the current era of the game, the game’s beginner to intermediate towers aren’t completely useless, they actually serve their purpose. Back in the 2021 era though? If you bought Militant, Rocketeer, and Paintballer, congratulations, you find out that all your grinding was for nothing.

The Abundance of Bugs
The next major issue is that this era was RIDDLED with bugs.&nbsp; You have many bugs that were completely ignored by the devs until the next update that would come within months. A few examples are Pursuit and Ace Pilot not being immune to stuns, Medic’s stun cleanse ability doing nothing at all, and many visual bugs regarding cosmetics of the towers. The tower bugs stayed, hindering the tower for months, while the visual bugs were just annoying but seeing them stay for over a year from Overhaul to Solar Eclipse was really dumb since these were so easy to fix.&nbsp;

And then there are towers getting released into the game while still having their own major bugs. Toxic Gunner is one clear example. Back in its release, this tower was able to slow down every enemy in the game by 50%, PERMANENTLY. Equipping this tower basically made the game a free win (for the most part). This was fixed 2 months later, but the aforementioned Pursuit/Ace Pilot and Medic bugs stayed until Solar Eclipse 5 months later.

Once Toxic Gunner was fixed, players resorted to other ways to break the game. The Military Base bug. This was actually in the game for quite a while now but didn’t receive widespread attention until Toxic Gunner was patched. This was then fixed 2-3 weeks later.&nbsp;

And because of how bad the game’s balancing was, players had to use these game breaking bugs just to beat Hidden Wave/Hardcore. The Overhaul Era didn’t really have this issue, you could still beat those two perfectly fine with legitimate strategies, but when Frost Invasion came, Hardcore was made harder because the intended price inflation mechanic was fixed for placement costs. When you were struggling to beat Hardcore, all you had to do for most of the game was just abuse these game-breaking bugs.&nbsp;

Right after the Military Base bug was fixed, there was another bug players discovered to abuse. Holding the Minimize/Maximize button of your Roblox tab, this made the game freeze and not let you join into a game until you let go of the button, and by doing this, if there was already one player in the game, then you joined right after the round starts, the rest of the game would give you the wave bonus as if it were a solo game. This was then fixed 2 months later in September.

I get that the devs had to be quick on fixing bugs that give you free wins, but there’s no reason for them to NOT have fixed the aforementioned other tower and visual bugs.

If players are abusing bugs that were never intended to exist, solely because these are the best ways to beat hard gamemodes, that is more than “harmless.” It’s bad game design.

The Elevators
A more minor issue people have overlooked is that matchmaking/parties did not exist at all in this era. (it was actually added on Solar Eclipse, but that was only for the event itself) Do you remember how annoying it was when you had to spend so much time actually getting on a solo game because there were so many randoms infesting your elevator? You could solve this by using a Private Server.. Which costs robux. Not all players have that.
Do you know how convenient the party system is right now? It still has its limitations on public servers, only letting you veto once, that is still much better than the elevator hell that infested most of the game up to 2023. No wonder people don’t miss elevators being the main way to join/start games.

Nostalgia
This is probably the biggest reason why this era of the game has been so glorified.&nbsp; Many players who are new to a game often find the era they first started playing in, their favorite era. That’s completely understandable.&nbsp;
Let me tell you one thing. The memories were good, that doesn’t mean the game itself was actually good. I first started playing TDS way back in 2019, I have a lot of happy memories and nostalgia, getting home from school, then immediately hopping on the game, not a single worry in the world, but that doesn’t mean the game was flawless. The same applies to 2021.

Even with all of my&nbsp; points bashing on the 2021 TDS era, I still have a lot of memories of just hopping on Roblox for hours after online class. I was grinding the Frost Invasion battlepass, beating Hidden Wave many times with a trusted group of friends, Summer 2021 for me was just a really enjoyable time. Underneath all of that happiness though, at the time, I still found it hard to ignore the massive issues the game had in this era. Many people in the community were complaining about easy-to-fix bugs staying for months, along with many of the towers just being bad.&nbsp; I don’t let all my nostalgia of 2021 TDS completely blind me to all the problems it had.

Current Era of the game
Before anyone interprets this post as me defending everything about the modern era of the game, I can also say it also has absolutely legitimate criticisms, stemming from the game’s excessive power creep, abundance of progression, too much monetization, etc. I agree. I don’t play the game much anymore these days because all they’re adding is just more and more content that feels really tedious to grind for, but when you look back at earlier eras that had massive issues as well…

I’m not arguing 2021 TDS was absolutely horrible, you can enjoy the older events, gameplay, community, that’s completely valid. Solar Eclipse is still my favorite event to this day.&nbsp; The main reason why I made this post is because I’ve seen some people outright say the 2021 TDS was peak, and completely dismiss all of its issues, while also saying “modern era bad” without any constructive arguments.&nbsp;

Each era has its own issues. 2021 TDS can have memories and a simpler time but has many issues regarding bugs and balancing, while the modern era can have more quality-of-life features, but has too many monetization and power creep issues. Neither era is “peak golden age”.&nbsp; It is more reasonable to acknowledge both era’s strengths and weaknesses.

So that finally concludes this long post. I hope you took your time to read all of this and understand my points. You are open to debate and criticize some of my points constructively.

